 "source_type": "instagram",
 "source_url": "https://www.instagram.com/reel/Ddtw-FgRdva/",
 "title": "CEO reveals #1 red flag in candidate interviews",
 "topic": "communication",
 "summary": "The creator discusses an interview scenario for a Director of Studio position to highlight a major red flag. Instead of faking knowledge, the creator values honesty and willingness to learn.",
 "key_points": [
  "A candidate with 20+ years of traditional experience claimed to be very good at YouTube and creator studios.",
  "When asked to show subscriber numbers for an interview with Kobe Bryant, the candidate fumbled and hesitated instead of admitting they did not know.",
  "A powerful and honest thing to say in an interview when you do not know something is: \"I don't know how to do it, but I will learn.\"",
  "Admitting what you do not know shows character and prevents you from bullshitting the interviewer who will find out later anyway."
 ],
 "content": "CEO reveals #1 red flag candidate interviews. What's a red flag you see in an interview where you say, I'll never hire this person? Red flag? Okay, so I'm hiring a guy for director of studio here. We already have a guy here, Justin. Same position. I'm interviewing a bunch of guys. And he comes in, and I say, so how much experience you got? He comes from the traditional NBC 20 years plus experience. I said, how good are you at YouTube? Oh, very good. I said, really, how familiar are you with creator studios? Very good, fantastic. I said, show me how many subscribers such and such interview with Kobe Bryant got. So he goes, well, uh, and he's just going like this. I said, why don't you just tell me you don't know? So then he comes and does the interview and guess what he says. I don't know, but I'll learn. Justin said that? Yes. Sometimes the most powerful thing you can say in a job interview, I don't know how to do it, but I will learn. That tells the interviewer, this is a person of character. Don't bullshit the interview, they're gonna find out later on anyway. Instagram reel/post by Valuetainment for Gen Z. Text / caption: Never do this in an interview. We’ve all been here … Truth above all 💡. Follow @vtgenz for more career and interview advice. #jobsearch #interview #internship #interviewtips",
